Read one section of a note and extract what it says.

Note: {{note}}

Section to read:
{{section}}

What the notebook already knows (for orientation, do not copy it into the output):
- similar notes: {{similar_notes}}
- entities that may be mentioned: {{candidate_entities}}
- open tasks: {{open_tasks}}
- topics: {{topics}}

Predicate vocabulary (use these CURIEs when one fits, else ex:snake_case):
{{vocabulary}}

Return a 1-3 sentence summary, the mentions (ref m1, m2, ...; name as written; kind; aliases seen; role in the note), the claims (subject and object are mention refs unless object_is_literal), the tasks opened or completed, the time references, and the topics.

Rules:
- Use only the note and the provided context; never invent entities or dates.
- Prefer reusing an existing entity when the candidate list contains it; create sparingly.
- Keep names as written by the author; put variants in aliases.
- Quote evidence verbatim; one claim per statement; no inferred hierarchy.
- When unsure whether two things are the same, answer `unsure` rather than guessing.
- Output JSON only, matching the schema.

